1
00:00:00,148 --> 00:00:03,888
(Sheldon:)opening the freezer and going,
"Aw, no strawberry."

2
00:00:03,885 --> 00:00:06,685
(Penny:)What about the girl
behind the counter?

3
00:00:06,688 --> 00:00:09,088
(Sheldon:)Hmm? Well, she spends
her whole day scooping.

4
00:00:09,090 --> 00:00:12,960
(Sheldon:)One arm's probably
bigger than the other.

5
00:00:12,961 --> 00:00:16,401
(Penny:)Is it possible you might not
actually want to meet someone?

6
00:00:17,999 --> 00:00:20,529
(Sheldon:)You are truly wise.

7
00:00:20,535 --> 00:00:21,315
(Penny:)Thank you.

8
00:00:21,338 --> 00:00:22,638
(Sheldon:)I'd say

9
00:00:22,637 --> 00:00:23,657
(Sheldon:)wise beyond your years,
but you're getting up there.

10
00:00:23,683 --> 00:00:24,913
(Penny:)All right.

11
00:00:26,107 --> 00:00:29,547
(Penny:)Come on. What is really
going on with you?

12
00:00:31,413 --> 00:00:34,213
(Sheldon:)Penny, I am going
to tell you a story

13
00:00:34,215 --> 00:00:35,485
(Sheldon:)that I've never told anyone.

14
00:00:35,483 --> 00:00:37,053
(Penny:)All right.

15
00:00:37,052 --> 00:00:39,382
(Sheldon:)I was 13 years old,

16
00:00:39,387 --> 00:00:42,387
(Sheldon:)and on spring break
from college.

17
00:00:46,361 --> 00:00:48,331
(Penny:)Not relating. Go on.

18
00:00:48,329 --> 00:00:52,729
(Sheldon:)I came home early because they
ran out of math to teach me.

19
00:00:52,734 --> 00:00:54,764
(Penny:)Oh, now I'm with ya. Okay.

20
00:00:54,769 --> 00:00:56,669
(Sheldon:)My mother was at bible study.

21
00:00:56,671 --> 00:00:59,301
(Sheldon:)I walked in the house
expecting to find it empty,

22
00:00:59,307 --> 00:01:03,147
(Sheldon:)and I heard a sound coming
from my parents' bedroom.

